{"name":"Yucatan White Habañero","hex":"#f2efe0","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"white","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Bright and colourless; reflecting equal quantities of all frequencies of visible light.","Of or relating to Europeans or those of European descent, regardless if their skin has cool or warm undertones."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The color of snow or milk; the color of light containing equal amounts of all visible wavelengths.","A person of European descent with light-colored skin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/white"},{"term":"habañero","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(hypercorrect) Nonstandard form of habanero."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/haba%C3%B1ero"}],"entries":[{"title":"Yucatán","blocks":[{"text":"Yucatán, officially the Free and Sovereign State of Yucatán, is one of the 31 states which, along with Mexico City, constitute the 32 federal entities of Mexico. It comprises 106 separate municipalities, and its capital city is Mérida."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/48/Templo_de_los_Guerreros.jpg/330px-Templo_de_los_Guerreros.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yucat%C3%A1n","wikidata":"Q60176"},{"title":"Habanero","blocks":[{"text":"The habanero is a pungent cultivar of Capsicum chinense chili pepper. Unripe habaneros are green, and they color as they mature. The most common color variants are orange and red, but the fruit may also be white, brown, yellow, green, or purple. Typically, a ripe habanero is 2–6 centimetres long. Habanero chilis are very hot, rated 100,000–350,000 on the Scoville scale. The habanero's heat, flavor, and floral aroma make it a common ingredient in hot sauces and other spicy foods."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/86/Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg/330px-Habanero_closeup_edit2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habanero","wikidata":"Q764375"},{"title":"White","blocks":[{"text":"White is the lightest color and is achromatic. It is the color of objects such as snow, chalk, and milk, and is the opposite of black. White objects fully reflect and scatter all the visible wavelengths of light. White on television and computer screens is created by a mixture of red, blue, and green light. The color white can be given with white pigments, especially titanium dioxide."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e2/Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg/330px-Delphinapterus_leucas_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White","wikidata":"Q23444"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG/500px-Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG/1280px-Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG/500px-Conflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AConflicto_Limitrofe_Yucatan_Campeche_Quintana_Roo.PNG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Chichen-Itza-Castillo-Seen-From-East.JPG/500px-Chichen-Itza-Castillo-Seen-From-East.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7a/Chichen-Itza-